  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "01",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m09p01-m09-p01-teaching-redo-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "a2e99a928411e7dd4038964b36e71d5718ab2cc72d5e751d19213346cbd3bd2d",
        "2": "196e077eecdfa4417c845a5806e0720a644d58a41f736efd35d0dfc214da01e1",
        "3": "edc87466b4a10e8e0678dab3661cccd2a3a30d1c465ad68ec4223ca9e24a7217"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s01-c1-0b097f5dec58",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "You'll learn when to use S three, what a completed write guarantees, and why a request can be denied. Start with the regional bucket. An A P I request names the bucket and the object's key.",
          "text_sha256": "0b097f5dec5840df12d40bec2a4cb6b060e1fda8bb7de0b11b79e5d7544e9beb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2acbe8d9c4bb92d5a9155bb5f1c927827281a02f89b1c5a1821cd61d9cc4a180",
          "asset_sha256": "a2e99a928411e7dd4038964b36e71d5718ab2cc72d5e751d19213346cbd3bd2d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s01-c2-7ab0407cf1ac",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The full key is images slash logo dot P N G. The slash marks a prefix, not a disk folder. The object contains the image bytes, metadata such as content type, and a storage class.",
          "text_sha256": "7ab0407cf1ac9c270f750fc09ab45163f5746a635da9ba36b19f1d23d50452d8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0bdfa142fc256be435137d9c0fae8218a6cf2fd24e562345ef8a8eea6fccd26e",
          "asset_sha256": "a2e99a928411e7dd4038964b36e71d5718ab2cc72d5e751d19213346cbd3bd2d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s01-c3-3405f2c93049",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Fetching a logo, a backup or a data-lake object fits this model. If an application needs POSIX file behavior or in-place block updates, choose another storage type before comparing storage classes.",
          "text_sha256": "3405f2c93049811e35d47b825aec8002c8e0e8200e7a658c1a5d635eae03c9be",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3405f2c93049811e35d47b825aec8002c8e0e8200e7a658c1a5d635eae03c9be",
          "asset_sha256": "a2e99a928411e7dd4038964b36e71d5718ab2cc72d5e751d19213346cbd3bd2d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s02-c1-20865058f8b7",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Follow orders slash one thousand one dot Jason into the bucket. Once put succeeds, a subsequent get can read the new object and list reflects the write. That is strong consistency: don't add a delay simply to make the write visible.",
          "text_sha256": "20865058f8b7257579c8547ad8664c77b75216a3ad5bcf92f3a278ca4fb25769",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dba26b2190c8f5e5d8afe96f5f73fce7721ef1d57fc376b47a9856e50e8e701b",
          "asset_sha256": "196e077eecdfa4417c845a5806e0720a644d58a41f736efd35d0dfc214da01e1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s02-c2-c2a3e4b25617",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Now two workers read the same E tag. If one changes the object, the other worker's If Match rejects its stale overwrite. Versioning preserves old versions for recovery; it doesn't settle the race.",
          "text_sha256": "c2a3e4b25617e88c5c047d943b8efface07f93924a9b6de61618b61ea4085278",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "155d78a1478b9e9ab0107446d2499bcafbace0ba1dd6f55521b957cd75384245",
          "asset_sha256": "196e077eecdfa4417c845a5806e0720a644d58a41f736efd35d0dfc214da01e1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s02-c3-e6798fd29399",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the order and payment are two objects, S three doesn't commit both as one transaction. Use a database transaction or a workflow designed to handle partial completion.",
          "text_sha256": "e6798fd29399f8ad3f2f76ff01d367691fabb7b92843b0916df016e17921b894",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b786f7a588f79816cb10893d9725b4711cc7728d3b1675df31ae406ead7795fa",
          "asset_sha256": "196e077eecdfa4417c845a5806e0720a644d58a41f736efd35d0dfc214da01e1"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s03-c1-3fba7f0bb3e2",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For Access Denied, follow the caller to the policy check. Suppose a role calls get object on the logo. Identify the exact role, action and key. An I A M identity policy can allow that read.",
          "text_sha256": "3fba7f0bb3e24e8135053901b67a493c9dc934dce65277ccfbad4cb1f0c92654",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9d3bf5b3161712d5fcfc9f05cf02d3cef5d9ffbbf99826b94c0de5dc93a93509",
          "asset_sha256": "edc87466b4a10e8e0678dab3661cccd2a3a30d1c465ad68ec4223ca9e24a7217"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s03-c2-d5cf96f05ea7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A bucket or access point policy may also apply. An explicit deny wins even when the role has an allow. Without a deny, still check that the effective permissions authorize the read.",
          "text_sha256": "d5cf96f05ea70ae45e306c8659b309dd1fa0a11d02fb03747f7f9381fa45eeda",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d5cf96f05ea70ae45e306c8659b309dd1fa0a11d02fb03747f7f9381fa45eeda",
          "asset_sha256": "edc87466b4a10e8e0678dab3661cccd2a3a30d1c465ad68ec4223ca9e24a7217"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p01-redo-s03-c3-503e5200eaf5",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If the bucket uses Bucket owner enforced, the bucket owner owns the objects and A C Ls are disabled. Adding an A C L won't fix this denial. Return to the exact principal, action, resource and policies in force.",
          "text_sha256": "503e5200eaf51d008b00a3eb8b4455f619d820e79c8761bb83a3a0a1d652901b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "062e40565a7caa8cdd7b76efc033f1f7254eb791f71a059e25e12e162bdc9d2d",
          "asset_sha256": "edc87466b4a10e8e0678dab3661cccd2a3a30d1c465ad68ec4223ca9e24a7217"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
